  evidence:
  - evidence_type: CURATOR_JUDGMENT
    source: https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=414; https://togomedium.org/medium/M412
    notes: 'JCM414 explicitly dissolves phosphate salts, ammonium chloride and thiosulfate
      in 500 ml water separately from calcium/magnesium and other additions. Source
      transcription basis (literal input amounts, not calculated stock concentrations):
      Distilled water: 500 ml; KH2PO4: 1 g; NH4Cl: 1 g; K2HPO4: 1 g; Na2S2O3・5H2O:
      1.55 g. No batch-to-final-volume conversion is made. Handling atmosphere is
      not listed as a material part; pH reagents are source inputs, without an assertion
      of unchanged molecular species after pH adjustment. Nested formulations remain
      source-qualified named parts where exact composition/owner identity is not established.
      No verified exact eligible ontology term or existing whole-preparation owner
      was established by the bounded source/owner review. This self-registry mapping
      represents the preparation, not its individual constituents.'
